f craft on display here that  warrants pouring over every square inch  as fans are well aware Rio is not afraid  of striking up a conversation with  anyone who cares to listen which in  shenmue's case is practically everyone  the NPC's of Shenmue 3 are many and  memorable from scrappy little kids with  a pawn shop the Tai Chi to craggy old  kung fu masters with lustrous white  eyebrows  unlike the environments the character  art style veers away from photo realism  and steers closer to caricature allowing  for a welcomed diversity of faces and  body types somewhat ironically this  serves to contribute to the overall air  of authenticity honestly I don't think  your kung fu is strong enough  although he's been studying martial arts  since he was seven Rio still has plenty  to learn and China has a lot to teach  him by visiting various schools and  encountering masters you're able to pick  up and develop a range of new techniques  sometimes you'll simply be perfecting  your Bruce Lee style one-inch punch  against the wooden training dummy but  often you'll be trying to land moves on  human opposition in a bid to improve  their efficacy and upgrade Rio's core  skills all that training is intended to  get Rio ready for the real world where  enemies and disciples of his archrival  landy on lining up to bruise that pretty  face of his Shenmue threes combat is  rebuilt from the ground up  but the influence from you Suzuki's  previous work is still evident and not  necessarily limited to his experience in  fighting games in a sly nod to the  racing franchise that first drew suzuki  to the world's attention players can  choose between automatic transmission  and manual transmission the former  automates combo strings for the benefits  of players who are more concerned with  enjoying the story while manual leaves  everything in your hands Rio will pick  up a number of new styles to sit  alongside the moves he picks up in the  previous two games and will have to make  strategic use of everything in his  arsenal to counter his rivals deadly  techniques  and finally Shenmue 3 couldn't call  itself a Shenmue game if it wasn't  filled with engrossing minigames and  compelling diversions all designed to  distract Ryo from his grand quest this  it knows all too well as within minutes  of entering bilú Ryo will happen upon  his first capsule toy machines a true  Shenmue signature soon after he's  goading into gambling away what little  he has on dice vintage pachinko boards  and even turtle races as he continues to  explore you'll also discover some  incredibly retro arcade games including  the returning reflex testing favourite  QTE title you can experience the  long-awaited third chapter of Ryo  hazuki's quest for vengeance when  Shenmue 3 releases on PlayStation 4 and  the epic game store on November 19  [Music]

